# Component Development Guidelines

## 🎯 Component Categories & Responsibilities

### Common Components (`components/common/`)
Reusable utility components that can be used across the application:

#### Modal Components
- **AlertDialogComponent**: Standard alert/confirmation dialogs
- **ConfirmationDialogComponent**: User confirmation prompts
- **FileUploadModalComponent**: File upload interactions
- **RestartModalComponent**: System restart confirmations

#### Form Components  
- **NumberInputDebounceComponent**: Debounced numeric input
- **RangeSliderComponent**: Custom range slider controls
- **TimeDropdownComponent**: Time selection dropdown

#### Display Components
- **ChartComponent**: Data visualization using Chart.js
- **PaginationComponent**: Table pagination controls
- **ProgressBarComponent**: Loading and progress indication
- **QuickviewComponent**: Side panel quick views

### Core Components (`components/core/`)
Feature-specific business logic components:

#### Data Management
- **AssetReadingsComponent**: IoT asset data display
- **DashboardComponent**: Main analytics dashboard
- **ConfigurationManagerComponent**: System configuration
- **LogsComponent**: System and application logs

#### Administration
- **UserManagementComponent**: User account management
- **CertificateStoreComponent**: SSL certificate management
- **BackupRestoreComponent**: System backup operations
- **NotificationsComponent**: Alert and notification management

### Layout Components (`components/layout/`)
Application shell and navigation components:
- **NavbarComponent**: Top navigation bar
- **SideMenuComponent**: Collapsible sidebar navigation
- **FooterComponent**: Application footer
- **LoginComponent**: Authentication interface

## 🏗️ Component Structure Standards

### File Organization
Each component follows the standard Angular structure:
```
component-name/
├── component-name.component.ts      # Component logic
├── component-name.component.html    # Template
├── component-name.component.css     # Styles
├── component-name.component.spec.ts # Unit tests
└── component-name.module.ts         # Module (if applicable)
```

### Component Class Structure
```typescript
@Component({
  selector: 'app-component-name',
  templateUrl: './component-name.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./component-name.component.css']
})
export class ComponentNameComponent implements OnInit, OnDestroy {
  // 1. Public properties (component state)
  public isLoading = false;
  public data: DataType[] = [];
  public selectedItem: DataType | null = null;
  
  // 2. Form controls (if applicable)
  public form: FormGroup;
  
  // 3. ViewChild references
  @ViewChild('elementRef') elementRef: ElementRef;
  
  // 4. Input/Output properties
  @Input() inputProperty: string;
  @Output() outputEvent = new EventEmitter<any>();
  
  // 5. Private properties
  private destroySubject: Subject<void> = new Subject();
  
  // 6. Constructor with dependency injection
  constructor(
    private service: ServiceName,
    private router: Router,
    private alertService: AlertService
  ) {}
  
  // 7. Lifecycle hooks
  ngOnInit() {
    this.initializeComponent();
  }
  
  ngOnDestroy() {
    this.destroySubject.next();
    this.destroySubject.unsubscribe();
  }
  
  // 8. Public methods (template-accessible)
  public onButtonClick(): void {
    // Method implementation
  }
  
  // 9. Private methods (internal logic)
  private initializeComponent(): void {
    // Initialization logic
  }
}
```

## 🎨 Template Guidelines

### Template Structure
Organize templates with clear sections:

```html
<!-- Loading state -->
<div *ngIf="isLoading" class="loading-container">
  <app-progress-bar></app-progress-bar>
</div>

<!-- Main content -->
<div *ngIf="!isLoading" class="content-container">
  <!-- Header section -->
  <div class="header">
    <h1 class="title">{{ pageTitle }}</h1>
    <div class="actions">
      <button class="button is-primary" (click)="onAction()">
        Action
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>
  
  <!-- Data display -->
  <div class="data-section">
    <div *ngFor="let item of data; trackBy: trackByFn" 
         class="data-item">
      {{ item.name }}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Error state -->
<div *ngIf="hasError" class="error-container">
  <app-alert type="error" [message]="errorMessage"></app-alert>
</div>
```

### Bulma CSS Integration
Use Bulma classes consistently:

```html
<!-- Container structure -->
<div class="container">
  <div class="columns">
    <div class="column is-8">
      <!-- Main content -->
    </div>
    <div class="column is-4">
      <!-- Sidebar content -->
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Form styling -->
<div class="field">
  <label class="label">Field Label</label>
  <div class="control">
    <input class="input" type="text" [(ngModel)]="value">
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Button styling -->
<button class="button is-primary is-loading" 
        [class.is-loading]="isProcessing"
        (click)="onSubmit()">
  Submit
</button>
```

## 🔄 Component Communication

### Parent-Child Communication
```typescript
// Child component
@Input() data: DataType;
@Output() dataChange = new EventEmitter<DataType>();

// Parent template
<app-child-component 
  [data]="parentData"
  (dataChange)="onDataChange($event)">
</app-child-component>
```

### Service-Based Communication
For complex state sharing, use services:

```typescript
// In component
constructor(private sharedService: SharedService) {}

ngOnInit() {
  this.sharedService.data$
    .pipe(takeUntil(this.destroySubject))
    .subscribe(data => {
      this.handleDataUpdate(data);
    });
}
```

## 🎯 Performance Best Practices

### Change Detection Optimization
- Use OnPush change detection strategy for pure components
- Implement trackBy functions for *ngFor loops
- Avoid complex calculations in templates

### Memory Management
- Always unsubscribe from observables in ngOnDestroy
- Use takeUntil pattern for subscription management
- Avoid memory leaks with proper cleanup

### Bundle Optimization
- Lazy load feature modules where appropriate
- Use dynamic imports for large dependencies
- Optimize images and assets